course: dictionary
lesson: 13798
title: Investing: giving now to gain later
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Investing means putting something in now, hoping it will bring back more later. Most often it is money. «Dad is investing his savings in shares.» He puts his money into shares because he hopes it will grow.
explain: Investing can also mean giving time or effort. «Ella is investing hours of practice in her violin.» She is not paid for the practice. She practises because she expects it to be worth it later, when she plays better.
explain: The clues help you work out the meaning. Look for words like shares, savings, future or practice. Then ask: is this person giving something now so they get more later? If yes, investing means the same kind of thing.
fact: Investing means putting money or time into something, hoping it will grow or be worth it later.
fact: «Investing» is the -ing form of the verb «invest».
fact: Money put into shares or property can go down as well as up, so investing has a risk.
fact: «Investing time» means spending time on something because you expect it to be worth it.
fact: Investing is not the same as spending: spending gives something back now, while investing waits for a return later.
exercise: «Dad is investing his savings in shares, hoping they will grow.» What does investing mean here? | Counting money in a bank | Hiding money under the bed | Spending money on sweets today | *Putting money into something to make more money later
exercise: «Ella is investing hours of practice in her violin.» What does investing mean here? | *Giving time now because it should pay off later | Wasting time on something useless | Forgetting her violin for a week | Playing very loudly
exercise: Why is investing money a risk? | Because banks close every day | *Because the money can fall as well as grow | Because shares are always free | Because money cannot be counted
test: «Mia is investing in a flat, hoping its value will rise.» Which word is closest in meaning to investing here? | Losing | *Putting money in | Hiding | Spending
test: «Tom is investing time in learning to swim.» What is Tom doing? | Swimming for fun only | Paying someone to swim for him | *Spending time now so he can get better later | Forgetting how to swim
exam: «Sam keeps investing in his future by saving a little every week.» What does the sentence show? | Sam has forgotten to save | *Sam is giving something up now to gain later | Sam is spending all his money today | Sam has lost all his money
